o 9).  M2.3: Two-Digit Numbers without Regrouping (Understand place value: tens and ones up to 99).M2.4: Addition using Indigenous Forest Produce (Add collections of local seeds, fruits, and leaves up to 20 — the entry in your mockup).Grade 3 (Proficiency Level)L3.1: Fluent Passage Reading with Comprehension (Read age-appropriate text at 60 WPM with understanding).L3.2: Dual-Script Sentence Sequencing (Reorder scrambled tribal words into Subject-Object-Verb word order).L3.3: Reading with Expression & Dialogue (Differentiate question, exclamation, and statement intonation).L3.4: Bilingual Passage Translation Check (Match short paragraph meanings between Hindi and the tribal language).M3.1: Two-Digit Addition & Subtraction with Regrouping (Solve daily village market/haat numerical scenarios).M3.2: Three-Digit Number Sense (Read, write, and compare numbers up to 999).M3.3: Equal Grouping & Intro to Multiplication (Divide objects into equal clusters; repeated addition).  M3.4: Simple Measurement & Local Units (Compare lengths and weights using non-standard village metrics).Complete Drop-In JSON Registry (All 24 Competencies)Provide this exhaustive JSON array to your agent to replace app/src/main/assets/schemas/nipun_curriculum_registry.json. It populates every option across Grades 1, 2, and 3:JSON[
